{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And there you shall serve elohim.</b> Israel in exile who serve idolatry involuntarily — they serve it בְּטָהֳרָה (under duress) (Avodah Zarah 8a)." "<b>Which do not see.</b> For they possess no volitional faculty, as their worshippers supposed — that the craftsmen make forms using tools of volitional action, to indicate that that primordial cause they imagined produces all those actions at will, and they would worship it and pray to it, to achieve that it should will to grant the requests of its worshippers. But in truth, no existent being other than HaShem, blessed be He, and man in his lifetime, possesses any volitional faculty; rather, all actions other than theirs proceed by an ordered nature assigned to them by HaShem, blessed be He."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:27.990729901Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}